\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\f0\fs24\cf0
\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri shuffled onto Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s white wood, elevated veranda. This wide veranda trimmed the long length of Vigram\u8217\'92s squat mansion. It was the quintessential rich man\u8217\'92s veranda in that it showed no signs of use. And it was indulgent, professing a mastery of craft which was completely unnecessary because the only people who could properly appreciate the clean, even lines, the dressed edges, the seamless transitions between plank and post, were the craftsmen themselves.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Some expert carpenter had gone to great lengths to hide the fact that he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d used of nails. Why?  Every nail head on every plank was plugged over by a dot of wood.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 It was a sign of some psychosis, as though the carpenter desperately needed to the world to believe that he didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t assemble this veranda with his effort, no, he\u8217\'92d pulled it whole out of the realm of idealized forms. The amount of gratuitous. Mandri, it was simply well-built. The stout boards under his feet were firm in their seats, and the bulky joinery of the overhead trellis supported a thick mat of leafy vine. And this , because as impressive as the veranda was, nature was still more compelling. The broad leaves of the vines were the most luxurious sun-shade, for they cast a bluish, dappled shadow over the deck while their bottoms glowed a bright lime green, a saturated green, a green so intense it soured Mandri\u8217\'92s mood because it reminded him, again, of colors that were impossible to paint.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He stared up at all that saturated green because the leaves seemed to pulse. He took it to be a sign that the high coming on strong. If he was lucky, and the burgeon he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d eaten was especially strong, then in about a finger\u8217\'92s time the fiddleback pattern in the trellis wood would start to shimmer. In half a hand, his mind\u8217\'92s eye would start to see all that leafy green bleed into the wood, and into the interstitial splotches of blue sky. These shapes and colors would all swirl together into one solid, flexing sheet that pulsed and breathed like an animal.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 This veranda would have been the perfect place get high, if only it were enclosed. As it was, the veranda\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s long, spindly balustrade did little to disguise the horror of Vigram\u8217\'92s leech farm.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Twelve, massive, man-made lakes tiled Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s large estate, each lake a perfect square, each lake filled with so many leeches that they crossed that threshold from a collection of individuals to a force of nature. They were swarms. They were undulating clouds of mud. The edges of the nearest lakes were lined with roofless stalls, with each stall penning a live animal into the shallows. Goats, horses, cows; any animal larger than a large dog would do. The larger animals were slumped onto support beams, with snouts tied into bags of intoxicating freeweed smoke. This was not an act of beneficence to inure them to the pain, it was Vigram\u8217\'92s way of keeping his peaceful country air free of their wild moaning.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The rest of the estate was mostly flies and marshgrass. The sky was cloudy with the kind of tall, mountainous clouds that swallowed landscape paintings whole, the kind that cast broad shadows down upon the world to pull the viewer through the distance, as they pulled Mandri now, all the way out to the sparkling blue line on the horizon which was the sea.}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1  And that sparkle was especially bright, rivaling the sun. The high from these down-valley burgeons could make textures slide and edges bleed, but the chief effect was that anything bright would sparkle and shimmer\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the sunlit cloudrims, the seashine, every bright line and specular reflection would tighten up and sparkle like a twinkling star.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I made this myself,\u8221\'94 Vigram said as he unfolded a tall, blocky easel. He was referring to the easel, not the veranda, but even so Mandri doubted it, because the easel was also well-made. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I brewed the glue,\u8221\'94 Vigram said proudly, \u8220\'93hammered the fittings. I should say that it\u8217\'92s my creation, but that feels\u8230\'85indulgent.\u8221\'94 He grabbed the easel by the shoulders and admired the height of it, taller than himself by a good two heads.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you sure you want to do this here?\u8221\'94 Mandri asked as he leaned against a trellis post.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why not here?\u8221\'94 said Vigram.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri eyed the distressed animals in the lakes below. The poor things were shaved down to the pink skin like criminals, reduced to bags of blood. Leechmen waded between the stalls to trowel off the largest leeches and toss them into grass baskets. Those leeches which weren\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t engaged in the constant struggle for the cleanest spot of flesh were busy mating. It was a bit of an orgy down there.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri wanted nothing more than to get away from the sight and smell of all that torture, but he couldn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t admit that, for fear of offending Vigram. Besides, he\u8217\'92d eaten more than his fill of Meskalimi leech, so all those goats, horses, and cows were suffering in leech paradise on account of him. What right did he have to look away?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Disgusted with his own complicity, he looked away and fumbled about for an excuse to change locale.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93These vines are thick,\u8221\'94 he finally said, \u8220\'93but not quite thick enough for a solid shadow. A dappled light will fall upon the sitter, and that will make things difficult.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He held his hand out and turned it through the invisible shafts of light to demonstrate the effect.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93My dear Mandriiii,\u8221\'94 Vigram said with a patronizing drawl. \u8220\'93The patterns of light and shadow are a magical vesture.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, we can worry about magical vestures when we\u8217\'92ve mastered the basics.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No,\u8221\'94 Vigram said firmly, long beard wiggling. \u8220\'93I won\u8217\'92t have it any other way. A magical vesture for a magical subject.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 As if bidden from the heavens by Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s words, two young men hauled a marble bust of Vigram\u8217\'92s head out onto the veranda. Mandri wouldn\u8217\'92t have recognized the bust as Vigram if Vigram\u8217\'92s name weren\u8217\'92t engraved into the base. It was not so much an idealized version of the man as it was a lie, with less fat in the cheeks. And it had hair. It didn\u8217\'92t go so far as to proclaim a full flow of wavy locks, but there was, undeniably, a slight impression of curly hair haloing the skull. The beard was much shorter, and trimmed close to a well-defined jaw, and the brow had an imperious aspect. In short, he was styled in the fashion of an early Hrkan Lord, a warrior-king. The only thing it was missing was a Lordly crown.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You look confused,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m not,\u8221\'94 Mandri said quickly. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m only\u8230\'85I guess\u8230\'85I mean, it\u8217\'92s your choice of subject, of course. You will paint what you want to paint.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But I\u8217\'92m not painting,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, perplexed. \u8220\'93Mandri, you are here to give a demonstration. I know you didn\u8217\'92t bring any materials, so I\u8217\'92ve plenty here.\u8221\'94 He knuckle-knocked the top of a square taboret a slave had set up next to the easel. He pulled one of the drawers out to show Mandri the packed rows of little clay jars. \u8220\'93Paints, brushes, turpentine,\u8221\'94 he said, pointing them out. \u8220\'93Linseed. I\u8217\'92ve a safflower and clove dip here, my own concoction\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 it will keep the brushes wet in the event we move into an extended session. Everything\u8217\'92s here. Nothing but the best.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I see\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 Mandri muttered. He crossed his arms and pinched his lip. \u8220\'93You want me to watch me paint?\u8221\'94 he asked, hoping he\u8217\'92d misunderstood something.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, a little perplexed, as if this were all agreed upon beforehand. And perhaps it had been. Mandri could hardly recall replying to Vigram\u8217\'92s invitation, because he\u8217\'92d been drunk on burgeon hooch at the time. The burgeon was strong then, and it was coming on strong now. He couldn\u8217\'92t stop staring at Vigram\u8217\'92s long brown beard because all that hair was sort of transforming into an active mudslide. There was every chance, that in half a finger, he might not be able to recognize his own hand even if he held it right in front of his face. These down-valley burgeons could duplicate things\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 this didn\u8217\'92t happen often, but when it did, he could not find his hand amidst a splay of twenty or so hands, all with their pinkies and thumbs melting in and out of each other.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He had eaten the burgeon on the assumption that Vigram would be the one painting. If he were staring over Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s shoulder, he could easily fluff his way through a lesson by mixing a few compliments into the slew of general tips and structural advice that were applicable to any beginner. But to actually paint? The white wood planks under his feet were starting to bend and breathe. How was he supposed to draw a straight line, or keep things in proportion, if the wind itself could send the entirety of his visual field all astir?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I need to know where you\u8217\'92re at,\u8221\'94 he finally said. \u8220\'93I mean, I haven\u8217\'92t seen you paint. So, for this first lesson, I would prefer to watch. If I\u8217\'92m going to tailor my instruction, I need to know your skill level.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No,\u8221\'94 Vigram said sharply. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll be honest, Mandri\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 I\u8217\'92m skeptical of your ability. You are skilled, yes, but you\u8217\'92re skilled in such a way that doesn\u8217\'92t matter. I hope you understand my meaning.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I don\u8217\'92t,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, genuinely confused.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oh, how should I say this?\u8221\'94 Vigram said as he stared at the ceiling of vines. He sort of squeezed and clenched the air, as though his hands needed to grasp his idea before he could speak it.\u8220\'93You aren\u8217\'92t\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 he opened his hand and aerated the air near his nose. \u8220\'93You aren\u8217\'92t an }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 artist}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 ,\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 he finally said. \u8220\'93Not in the way that I define it. You do make pretty pictures, but none of them are inspired. Of course, I haven\u8217\'92t seen your entire body of work, but from what I }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 have}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  seen\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8230\'85I\u8217\'92ll simply say that I feel comfortable assuming that you\u8217\'92ve never transcended the boundary of the possible. I should say more than that, because I suspect that you agree with me, and that you view it as a great shortcoming, and this gnaws at you, evidenced by the manner of your grooming. I should say\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 neglectful.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 unkempt hair, his stubbly chin, his skinny neck, the flea-bag that is your robe. What is that homespun nonsense? It\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s waste material. The comfort with which you wear it is embarrassing.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri searched Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s face for a glint of sarcasm, but the man seemed eager, if not serious. Mandri moved past it and said, \u8220\'93Look, if I\u8217\'92m going to instruct you, then you need to let me instruct you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93If you intend to be paid,\u8221\'94 Vigram said with a prodding glare, \u8220\'93then you need to do what I say and show me something worth seeing.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But nobody learns by }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 watching}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 ,\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 Mandri moaned. \u8220\'93You learn by doing. I mean, the fact that you even want me to teach you at all, or think that you can steal what I do\u8230\'85Look, you don\u8217\'92t want to know how }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 I}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  paint a face. You need to figure out how }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 you}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  paint a face. If you only copy the way that I paint, then you\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92re not learning. You\u8217\'92re not growing into yourself as an artist. In five years, you\u8217\'92ll look at your own work and realize that you haven\u8217\'92t done a damned thing but waste your time copying someone else.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, Mandri, Mandri,\u8221\'94 Vigram clucked. \u8220\'93I wonder if you can hear yourself. Next, you\u8217\'92ll speak of }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 styles}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 .  \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91Grow into myself as an artist\u8217\'92? Nonsense. A man communes with the divine, or he does not. Now, let\u8217\'92s have no more of this degeneracy.\u8221\'94 He turned and lifted a pure white, stretched canvas up onto the easel. The corner of the clean sheet sparkled in Mandri\u8217\'92s eye.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You will stand here,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, \u8220\'93and I will watch you paint. You will articulate your decisions as you make them. I will ask clarifying questions as they come. If you don\u8217\'92t want to do that, then you will leave. Will you stay, or will you leave?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oh, I\u8217\'92ll stay,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, and he gave a cheeky grunt, as though he were graciously conceding instead of being flushed out. \u8220\'93But you need to understand that I\u8217\'92m not going to be able to articulate everything I do. There\u8217\'92s more than twenty years of practice going into every stroke. It won\u8217\'92t be all that helpful. And you\u8217\'92re not going to improve unless you paint.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I know it,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, \u8220\'93Better than you, I should say. But for now, }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 you}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  will paint. Now, before we begin\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 he drew back and shouted over his shoulder, \u8220\'93Someone quiet that animal!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 An old, yellow headed ox was mooing down in the nearest leech lake. It was angry at being stuck inside its stall, and also, at being bled to death. It mooed again. It bucked against its restraints, then gave a desperate, plaintive plea: \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mrruuuuuu!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Get that beast\u8217\'92s snout stuck in some weed!\u8221\'94 Vigram roared. Down below, a few leechmen stumbled out of their marshgrass daydreams. They adjusted their wide-brim hats, and scurried towards the ox. They splashed into the belly-deep water, and the burgeon had all that splashing sparkling like a spill of diamonds.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri sighed a sigh for the old ox. He wished he had the courage to moo like that. He privately resolved to never eat a Meskalimi leech again. Then he did what he was told to do. He pulled the paints and solvents out of the taboret, set up a standard pallette of warms and cools, then started at that white canvas as though it were an old enemy. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram took up his post behind Mandri, and sort of loomed over Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s shoulder. \u8220\'93I should say, that I don\u8217\'92t care about the image, not exactly. I want to see your breathing technique, so to speak\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 I want to see your way of being inspired, how you breathe in vision of the divine, and then how you transmute that vision in to this physical world.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram, I\u8217\'92m not that kind of painter,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The first exploratory marks were always difficult. Every work of art must be built on a firm foundation; get it wrong and everything that comes after will be wrong as well. Unfortunately for Vigram, he had that all too common beginner\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s habit of refusing to use his god damned brain. He started drawing wherever his hand happened to land, and whatever happened next was up to Solraheen. The end result was that Pel\u8217\'92s head was half the size it needed to be. It was also too left-of-center. There\u8217\'92d be an awkward expanse behind her healthy sweep of hair.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hold on,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re moving too fast.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri looked at the oval he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d drawn. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You need to tell me what you\u8217\'92re thinking,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, I\u8217\'92m not thinking of this as a portrait\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 not yet. All we have right now is an oval, a rectangular canvas, and where that oval sits on that canvas. All I\u8217\'92m doing is putting an oval on a rectangle.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Right.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So I\u8217\'92m thinking, where\u8217\'92s the best place to put that oval? How big should it be? I have the whole canvas here, and maybe I haven\u8217\'92t quite used it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92ve told me all this before.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram rubbed the marks away with his palm.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He stepped back.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He studied Pel.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He stepped again to the canvas, then scratched another black oval exactly where the first had been.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Is that better?\u8221\'94 Vigram asked with all the awareness of a potted plant. \u8220\'93You think it needs to be bigger?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why not,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, and he drew the oval again, but only slightly larger. From then on, every other mark he made was accompanied by a look back to Mandri for reassurance. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93How do you know,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, \u8220\'93when the mark you\u8217\'92ve made is correct?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93They\u8217\'92re never correct.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 There was a glimmer of understanding in Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eye, but just as soon as it came it faded. \u8220\'93If the mark is always wrong, then how can you ever move past it? You\u8217\'92ll be redrawing the same line over and over again.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You move on when you can\u8217\'92t stand to try anymore.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That sounds miserable.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It is,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, feeling understood. \u8220\'93You should be defeated by the time you\u8217\'92ve finished. I\u8217\'92ve always thought that you should never feel good about what you\u8217\'92re doing, because that means you\u8217\'92re not trying hard enough. Now, I\u8217\'92ll finish\u8230\'85I\u8217\'92ll finish the basic shapes.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Alright.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91finished\u8217\'92 the \u8216\'91basic shapes\u8217\'92. He looked to Mandri for final approval.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, I don\u8217\'92t have you here to watch you draw. I\u8217\'92m here to watch you paint.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0  \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But you need to understand the importance of the drawing. You\u8217\'92re always drawing. Even when painting, you are drawing.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I know,\u8221\'94 Vigram grumbled. \u8220\'93You talk about it all the time.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram made to redraw the too-large chin, but was interrupted by a loud, mournful ox bellow.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Damn it!\u8221\'94 Vigram cried, shaking his fist.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Focus,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. \u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t get distracted. Let your men do their job.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93If they were doing their job, I wouldn\u8217\'92t have heard that noise!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Please,\u8221\'94 Mandri repeated. \u8220\'93Focus.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram closed his eyes and took a deep breath. When he next looked upon his canvas, he was resolved: \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m done drawing! I\u8217\'92m here to paint!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He tossed his charcoal over his shoulder and picked up his favorite brush. He mixed a bluish shade of bronze\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the color of the jaw of a Jandri man who keeps a close shave\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and then he threw down the first splotches of color in a flurry. He wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t painting so much as he was assaulting the canvas. And Sol\u8217\'92s light, that bentberry fiber weave was innocent. Expensive, too, coveted for its depth of feeling, for how it made the undertones blush. Troubled by Vigram\u8217\'92s hand, those tones were bruised and near to bleeding. It was a very confused slapping around.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri had to look away.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He glanced in Pel\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s direction.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The moment his eyes wandered down the depth of her neckline, the corner of her lip perked up. He kept looking, because why else would she wear that cut if not to catch him staring? Why else would she be swimming in that perfume? Why bite that honeyed, aching lip? Why, if Solraheen\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s last will and testament was not inciting him to stare, why did the soft shadows of the vines overhead frame her piercing eyes with the most magnificent golden light? A magical vesture indeed. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, stop flirting with my muse.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I am not flirting,\u8221\'94 Mandri claimed. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m checking proportions.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes, and how are her proportions?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The old goat\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eyebrows jumped suggestively. Pel huffed in annoyance. The yellow headed ox weighed in with an oxen roar.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93MRRRRRUUUUUUUUUUUUU!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s it!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Below, in the leech lake, two leechmen tried to force the yellow-headed ox\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s snout into a bag of freeweed smoke. But the men were too skinny. The ox bucked them both into the air, then broke its constraints and jumped its rail. The beast tore through the leech lake, kicking up waves of confused, copulating leeches. Seeing this, Mandri\u8217\'92s spirit soared, and he clenched his fist in a quiet cheer.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Stop that ox!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted as he pointed with his loaded brush. \u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s a five silver-strings of leeches attached to that beast! If you don\u8217\'92t\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram,\u8221\'94 Mandri said firmly. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92ll make a bad habit if you keep stopping in the middle of the work.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t tell me what to do, boy! On }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 my}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  farm!?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Focus! Let it go.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram drew up in rage. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t ask me to let go of my principles! That animal }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 defies}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  me.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram rushed to a window in the trellis and ordered his men to greater action. A squad was gathered. They hunted as a pack. Vigram conducted their movements with his brush. They soon had the ox surrounded in the shallows of a distant lake. The ox, legs wide like a waterbug, fended off their sharpened sticks with its stubbed horns. Mooing, bleeding, fighting for its life, it charged the smallest leechman. The little man dove into the infested waters, and again, the ox was loose.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93DAMN IT ALL!\u8221\'94 Vigram screamed.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s chest swelled with both pity and admiration. Such feeling could not be tamed. He had to do something.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What if I bought it?\u8221\'94 he asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s rage was blunted by sheer confusion. He turned around.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri found his confidence and said, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll buy the ox off you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So that we can continue with the lesson. I\u8217\'92d like to get home before dark.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nonsense. We\u8217\'92ll come to it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m serious. I\u8217\'92ll buy it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That decrepit thing? Are you looking to sacrifice it? The gods are all dead, you know this. Are you making fun of me?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What? No.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Do you }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 judge}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  me, boy?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93This isn\u8217\'92t about you, Vigram. I respect the creature. It\u8217\'92s got fight.\u8221\'94}}